        "standfirst": "AFC Bournemouth beat Sunderland 2-0, the visitors down to 10 men after a first-half red card.",
        "account": "Marcus Tavernier put the Cherries in front after five minutes, heading Evanilson's pass straight down the middle. Sunderland lost Kevin Danso to a red card 12 minutes after Tavernier's goal, and Régis Le Bris's side were left a goal down and a man short.\nEvanilson doubled the lead just after half-time, left-footed from inside the box and through the middle. Chris Rigg went off injured for Sunderland midway through the second half.",
        "sections": [
          {
            "head": "Evanilson's goal and assist",
            "pitch": "The goal was Evanilson's second in the league this season, coming from six shots, and the league also paid him one point for defending.",
            "stake": "If anyone can, Bannan can has him, for 10 points against The Raccoons."
          },
          {
            "head": "Tavernier's fourth goal",
            "pitch": "That header took Tavernier to four for the league campaign, from three shots in the match, and his defending brought the full two points a match can pay.",
