        "standfirst": "Brighton & Hove Albion beat Crystal Palace 5-0, scoring three times in the first 10 minutes.",
        "account": "Jaydee Canvot put the ball into his own net after four minutes to give Brighton the lead. Diego Gómez added another three minutes after the own goal, taking Olivier Boscagli's pass on the break and striking it right-footed from more than 35 yards, high into the net. Charalampos Kostoulas then picked out Yasin Ayari, whose shot went low into the corner after 10 minutes and gave Brighton three goals in six minutes.\nKostoulas scored himself early in the second half, a low left-footed shot that found the corner. Jack Hinshelwood, on for Pascal Groß, completed the 5-0 six minutes from time, converting a corner from close range, right-footed into the top corner.",
        "sections": [
          {
            "head": "Boscagli, Kostoulas both supply",
            "pitch": "Boscagli's pass for Gómez's long-range goal was one of three chances he laid on across the match. Kostoulas supplied Ayari and then scored himself, taking four shots in all, and that strike was the third of his league season.",
            "stake": "Bayern Bru claimed Boscagli on Wednesday, for nine points; The Truffle Pigs has Kostoulas, for nine points against Bayern Bru."
          },
          {
            "head": "Ayari scores, Dunk defends",
            "pitch": "Ayari had four shots, and his strike brings his league goals for the season to two. Lewis Dunk was credited by the league with one defensive point, half of the most that a single match pays a man.",
            "stake": "domeitalycoach claimed Ayari on Friday, for 11 points; Hazza Maguazza's Redempshazza has Dunk, for seven points against domeitalycoach."
          }
